      "host_doing": "",
      "scene_key": "",
      "scene": "",
      "answer": "The doorway acts as an event boundary that files the old thought away, so the reason slips out of reach.",
      "loop_line": "Next time you freeze, blame the door. Why did I come in here?"
    },
    {
      "line": "Doorways quietly mess with your memory. Why?",
      "frame_one": "The host stands in a glowing open doorway, a small paper note drifting out of its mitten hand behind it.",
      "host_doing": "",
      "scene_key": "",
      "scene": "",
      "answer": "The doorway is an event boundary: the mind ends one scene there and files its contents away.",
      "loop_line": "Now you know why doorways quietly mess with your memory."
    },
    {
      "line": "Your forgetfulness might be the doorway's fault.",
      "frame_one": "The host points accusingly at a wooden doorframe while looking sheepish, a dropped shopping list lying at its feet.",
      "host_doing": "",
      "scene_key": "",
      "scene": "",
      "answer": "Research suggests walking through a doorway files the thought away, so the door gets some of the blame.",
      "loop_line": "Next time you blank, remember: it might be the doorway's fault."
    }
  ],
